# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows and runs on Linux in Docker. Git is
# configured with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout —
# fine for source files, fatal for anything Linux has to *execute*.
#
# entrypoint.sh with CRLF makes its shebang read "#!/bin/sh\r". Linux looks for
# an interpreter literally named "/bin/sh\r", does not find one, and the
# container crash-loops with the memorably unhelpful:
#
#     exec /app/entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
# The file is right there. It is the line endings.
#
# CI never saw this because GitHub's runners check out on Linux, where autocrlf
# does nothing. Only a Windows checkout produces the broken artefact — so the
# image built locally is broken while the one built by the server is fine.

# Anything Linux executes, or parses as a script, must be LF.
*.sh              text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh     text eol=lf
Dockerfile        text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile      text eol=lf

# Compose and CI files are read by Linux tooling; keep them LF for consistency.
*.yml             text eol=lf
*.yaml            text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png             binary
*.jpg             binary
*.jpeg            binary
*.webp            binary
*.pdf             binary
*.xls             binary
*.xlsx            binary
*.ico             binary
